{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>ועשית.</b> Now it is not written how thick the plank was, and the earlier authorities said it was one cubit. If so, the south wall was thirty cubits, and likewise the north. Now there remained in the west wall only a width of eight cubits, and we need to place there eight planks — perhaps they were needed per cubit, for the thickness was one cubit because of the middle bar that entered inside the plank. And according to the opinion of our master Solomon [Rashi], it stood by miracle, for by the plain sense there are three middle bars, and thus it is written מן הקצה אל הקצה [from end to end], not אל הקצות [to the ends]. And if it is a received tradition that the thickness was thus, we hear and accept. And if by way of reasoning, there is another arrangement: the two bars are upper, and likewise the lower ones are until half the wall, and the middle bar that was brought inside the planks would extend מן הקצה אל הקצה [from end to end]; and similarly לעשות בתוך התכלת ובתוך הארגמן (below 39:3) and likewise הפעמונים בתוך הרמונים (ibid. v. 25) — and were it not for this, the middle bars would not have been overlaid with gold. And if we say that we do not know how thick the plank was, we have to determine how the west was arranged. Now at first they would set up the west side, for the two planks that are למקצועות המשכן [for the corners of the tabernacle], which means like angles, and likewise חצי מקצוע החצר [half the corner of the court] was, for it was in the shape of an elongated quadrangle. Now we have corners, and these two planks alone that are at the corners are not like the measure of the planks mentioned; therefore Scripture distinguished them, and said כן יהיה לשניהם לבדם [so they shall be for the two of them alone] — not the other planks. And by these two planks they establish the tabernacle, and the six planks were in the middle. Now the width of the tabernacle was ten cubits, and we do not know whether the corner planks were square or round, for we have only one cubit. And according to the approach that our master Solomon said, these planks would not be in an even row, for half a cubit would be inside, for it is a plank and not a fabric, and afterward they would place the planks of north and south — now it would protrude outside the tabernacle by the thickness of the plank; therefore it would be opposite the pillar of the entrance of the tabernacle, and in half of the goatskin curtains would be the arrangement."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:45.108172360Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}